  body: "# Mandatory reconsideration in the captured DMG\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nFor the post-28 October
    2013 route described in the DMG, an application for revision is considered before the appeal right is exercised,
    with an express ESA pending-LCW-appeal exception.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe source contains different
    routes for decisions notified before and from 28 October 2013. Do not state that mandatory reconsideration is
    universally required or that its notice is itself a new outcome decision.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n\
    - [DMG 03012, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a212d2e58aae59498cb2a1a/dmg-vol-1-ch-3.pdf#page=5)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 3: Revision .\n- [DMG 06006, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a212d4adbcb60fc6ccb2a0c/dmg-vol-1-ch-6.pdf#page=4)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 6: Making appeals and staying.\n- [DMG 06007, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a212d4adbcb60fc6ccb2a0c/dmg-vol-1-ch-6.pdf#page=4)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 6: Making appeals and staying.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source is DWP guidance,
    not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication, not an official
    DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are one-based file
    positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships preserve
    extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current applicability
    remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch3` PDF SHA-256: `4aebcf1988fb7d96698dce77bf88d68272a5975171decc42f58c32cfa1d42eeb`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `444fa1a240db31b94cb75c13a2f2ece7c691f15aeca0bec2dd298e2f4e08f66a`.\n- `dmg-vol1-ch6`
    PDF SHA-256: `dcd2a7ede4499792d9bc6762c94a2d6c0ca6e811cb077abbbd4e41e4d405a4e4`; extracted pages SHA-256: `e95434f7e856adbd1c8550b369066644a6bf6aa7567af05a1d41768d3dae0c3e`.\n\
    \nThe publicly acquired chapter 6 PDF carries the printed footer “Official - DWP Use Only”. This observation
    is preserved alongside its public acquisition URL; the source owner should clarify any conflict with intended
    reuse. It is not evidence of access to unpublished material.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-revision
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The paragraph links the appeal gateway to an application for revision and sets out an exception
      and notice conditions.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch3/0005
      quote: "03012 Where the conditions are potentially met for an award of ESA pending a LCW appeal, mandatory\n\
        \nreconsideration is not required1 (see DMG 42810 - 42813). Decisions notified on or after 28.10.13 can\n\
        \nonly2 be appealed if the claimant has applied for a revision and the notice of the decision includes a\n\
        \nstatement to that effect. The claimant must be given a notice that informs them 3\n\n\n1. of the decision,
        whether as originally made or as revised and\n\n\n2. of the time limit for making an application for revision
        and\n\n\n3. that where the notice does not include a statement of reasons for the decision, the person may,
        within\none month of the date of notification of the decision, request that a written statement is provided
        for the\nreasons of the decision and\n\n\n4. that there is a right of appeal against the decision but that
        this can be exercised only if the Secretary\nof State has considered an application for revision.\n\n\n\
        Note: There is no time limit within which the DM must carry out the mandatory reconsideration. Once a\n\
        decision has been subjected to mandatory reconsideration, further dispute rights are not dependent\nupon
        a further mandatory reconsideration.\n\n\n                     1 [2020] EWHC 1999 (Admin); 2 SS CS (D&A)
        Regs, reg 3ZA(2); 3 reg 3ZA(1) & 3ZA(3)"
      locator: DMG 03012
  - target: term/dmg-first-tier-appeal
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The post-2013 appeal passage expressly associates reconsideration with appeal while preserving
      the ESA exception.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch6/0004
      quote: "06006 Where the conditions are potentially met for an award of ESA pending a LCW appeal, mandatory\n\
        \nreconsideration is not required1 (see DMG 42810 - 42813). For appeals lodged against decisions notified\n\
        on or after 28.10.13, claimants can only appeal to a FtT where the DM has first considered an application\n\
        \nfor revision of the original decision2 (see DMG Chapter 03: Revision). Where a claimant makes an appeal\n\
        before mandatory reconsideration has been requested then the appeal should be treated as a request\nfor
        a mandatory reconsideration.\n\n\n                             1 [2020] EWHC 1999 (Admin); 2 SS Act 98,
        s 12(3A); SS (D&A) Regs, reg 3ZA"
      locator: DMG 06006
